\section{State What the Reported Measurements Can Support}

Section~5.9 reports roughly \(12.35\) seconds for the five-stage CAS build and \(58.60\) for the HDL simulation build in the authors' setup. Those build measurements include compiling the emitted code, with the HDL path additionally including Chisel translation and Verilator. They are not measurements of a target processor's speed. The CAS was actually slower than the equivalent Verilator simulation in the reported three-stage runtime comparison (Section~5.7). The idealized memory used in these experiments and the demo library used for the hardware area comparison (Section~5.8) limit how directly those results transfer to another workload or physical implementation.
